# IdentityForge frontend build context (IF-V4-02, v5).
#
# The frontend Dockerfiles run `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`. Without
# this file, every build context carried the 99 shipped E2E
# screenshots (~27 MB) and — after a developer runs `npm ci` on a
# Windows host — the host's node_modules, which can overwrite the
# Linux container modules installed by `npm ci` and break
# architecture-specific native binaries. Local .env files, caches,
# reports and logs must never enter the image either.
#
# Kept in the context (the images need them): package.json,
# package-lock.json, src/**, e2e SPEC FILES (*.spec.ts), the
# Dockerfiles, docker-e2e-entrypoint.sh, index.html and configs.
# E2E screenshot OUTPUT goes to the mounted host path
# ./test-results/e2e-screenshots (docker-compose.test.yml) — it never
# depends on the pre-shipped PNGs in e2e/screenshots/.
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
e2e/screenshots/
e2e/.cache/
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git/
*.log
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*Zone.Identifier
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
